  "conduct": "The user comes back to close the measurement research out and says so in their first words. They remember a deep dive was running when they left, and when the session tells them what it found they take it as read — hold-or-weigh is the discussion's choice, not theirs today — and ask nothing back. They run the shop, not the search stack, and do not read code. Pressed at any point, the label-refresh question and whatever the dive opened travel with the topic, and the human-raters idea stays set aside for lack of budget. They are agreeable to required steps — a mandatory check gets a yes — and decline optional extras: no further dive, no measurement now, no new threads, and this is no dead end. They ask to wrap the research up and introduce no new material.",
